course: dictionary
lesson: 1123
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so you must read the scene to know which one is right. Take «Our car had a breakdown on the motorway.» Try the meaning in the sentence: our car stopped working on the motorway. That fits, so breakdown means a vehicle has stopped working.
explain: Now read «There was a breakdown in the talks, so the two sides went home.» Here breakdown means something has failed or ended. The clues are talks and went home. The same word can mean something different in each sentence, so do not stop at the first meaning you know.
explain: Breakdown can also be a list. «Mum read the breakdown of the costs: food, drinks and tips.» Here it shows the separate parts that make up a total. Always ask what the word is doing in the sentence, then try your meaning and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Breakdown is a noun, so you can have a breakdown or many breakdowns.
fact: «Breakdown» can mean a machine or vehicle has stopped working, as in «our car had a breakdown».
fact: «Breakdown» can also mean that something has failed or ended, as in «a breakdown in talks».
fact: «Breakdown» can mean a list showing the separate parts of a total, as in «a breakdown of the costs».
fact: In science, the breakdown of food means it splits into smaller parts. A breakdown truck is a vehicle that helps move a broken-down car.
exercise: «Our car had a breakdown on the motorway.» What does breakdown mean here? | A talk that failed | A list of costs | *A vehicle stopped working | A food bill
exercise: «There was a breakdown in the talks, so the two sides went home.» What does breakdown mean here? | A list of prices | *Something failed or ended | A pie chart of food | A car stuck on the motorway
exercise: «Mum read the breakdown of the costs: food, drinks and tips.» What is the breakdown here? | A machine that stopped working | The end of a holiday | A road jam with cars stopped on it | *A list showing the separate parts of a total
test: In science, what does the breakdown of food mean? | A bill with tips added | Food being thrown away | Food being bought at a shop | *Food splitting into smaller parts
test: On a motorway, after a breakdown, what should everyone do? | Run across the road to find help | *Get out and wait behind the barrier, away from the traffic | Drive faster to get away | Stay in the middle of the lane
exam: Which sentence uses breakdown to mean a list of parts? | The machine had a breakdown at school | The car had a breakdown on the hill | The talks had a breakdown and stopped | *Mum checked the breakdown of the bill: food, drinks and tips
